From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MrPowerGamerBR <git@mrpowergamerbr.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:15:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] SparklyPaper: Optimize "canSee" checks

Original project: https://github.com/SparklyPower/SparklyPaper
Ported from: https://github.com/Winds-Studio/Leaf

The "canSee" checks is in a hot path, invoked by each entity for each player on the server if they are in tracking range.

Use a fastutil map, check isEmpty() before containsKey, and give ChunkMap#updatePlayer a variant without the equals check, since updatePlayer already rejects the same entity.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/level/ChunkMap.java b/net/minecraft/server/level/ChunkMap.java
index fd0b9f20fbdd523d51550fd6009b5011e6e7e6e6..85096eed90d6e8dcc1fcc89996a5fb2ec63b9744 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/level/ChunkMap.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/level/ChunkMap.java
@@ -1431,7 +1431,7 @@ public class ChunkMap extends SimpleRegionStorage implements ChunkHolder.PlayerP
                     && ChunkMap.this.isChunkTracked(player, this.entity.chunkPosition().x(), this.entity.chunkPosition().z());
                 // Paper end - Configurable entity tracking range by Y
                 // CraftBukkit start - respect vanish API
-                if (visibleToPlayer && !player.getBukkitEntity().canSee(this.entity.getBukkitEntity())) { // Paper - only consider hits
+                if (visibleToPlayer && !player.getBukkitEntity().canSeeChunkMapUpdatePlayer(this.entity.getBukkitEntity())) { // Paper - only consider hits // SparklyPaper - optimize canSee
                     visibleToPlayer = false;
                 }
                 // CraftBukkit end
